# {{AGENT_NAME}} — Notion Project Agent (operations)

Watches Notion database `{{NOTION_DATABASE_ID}}` and reacts to page activity.
Event-driven — no cron, no servers to maintain. Installed by
[ai-automations](https://github.com/makasanaakshay/ai-automation-master);
re-run its installer to update (answers saved in `automation.config.json`).

```
Notion webhook (X-Notion-Signature, HMAC-SHA256 keyed with the verification token)
  → Cloudflare Worker relay            scripts/notion-agent/relay/worker.js
  → repository_dispatch                .github/workflows/notion-agent.yml
  → agent-run.sh                       restore state → resolve → playbook → save state
```

| Trigger | Playbook | Output (one Notion comment) |
|---|---|---|
| Page enters **{{STATUS_ANALYZE}}** | `analyze` | Options + trade-offs + recommendation, or numbered questions |
| Human comment on a {{STATUS_ANALYZE}} page | `respond` | Answer / updated proposal / remaining questions |
| Page enters **{{STATUS_IMPLEMENT}}** (or comment there) | `implement` | PR into `{{PR_BASE}}` — or questions if unclear |

State lives on the orphan branch `notion-agent-state` (`state/<page_id>.json`:
status_name, phase, last_comment_at, branch, pr_url). Notion events are
compact (entity id + type, no content), so every run re-fetches truth from
the API and diffs against saved state — payloads are only doorbells. Agent
comments are prefixed `{{AGENT_MARKER}} — `; the resolver skips marker
comments (loop protection). Comment recency is tracked by `created_time`
(ISO-8601). Page **content** edits are dropped at the edge — after editing a
page body, add a comment (or run manually) to re-trigger.

## Operating

- **Recover / backfill:** Actions → *Notion Project Agent* → *Run workflow* — empty `item_id` reconciles both watched statuses + tracked pages; a page id processes one.
- **Transcripts:** every run uploads `.agent-out/` as an artifact.
- **Model:** `CLAUDE_MODEL` in `scripts/notion-agent/env.sh` (currently `{{CLAUDE_MODEL}}`).
- **Pause:** disable (or delete) the webhook subscription in the integration settings (notion.so/profile/integrations → your integration → Webhooks).
- **Known blind spot:** moving a page back into a watched status silently — re-trigger with a comment or a manual run.

## Local dry-run (safe — needs NOTION_TOKEN exported)

```bash
DRY_RUN=1 bash scripts/notion-agent/agent-run.sh                 # reconcile scan
DRY_RUN=1 ITEM_ID=<page_id> bash scripts/notion-agent/agent-run.sh
```

## Guardrails

- Notion writes are **comments only** — the agent never changes the status property, never edits page bodies, never touches other properties; humans own the board.
- PRs are **always against `{{PR_BASE}}`** (branch `{{BRANCH_PREFIX}}/<kebab-slug>`); the agent never merges and never pushes to `{{PR_BASE}}` directly.
- `--dangerously-skip-permissions` only inside the disposable CI runner; local runs are `DRY_RUN` and stop before any AI call.
